#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Instrument for navigation and time to preview, for one or more file managers on one fixture.

  flea-field-nav calibrate [--delays 0,50,200] [--runs 10]   the shared method on tests/search-calib.qml
  flea-field-nav selftest                                    detector and key table over recorded logs, no display
  flea-field-nav preflight                                   core needs ok/MISSING, each entrant named, exit 0
  flea-field-nav measure PLAN.json                           run a plan: see measure()'s docstring for its JSON
  flea-field-nav report JSONL                                median [min..max] tables and ratios to Strata
  flea-field-nav explore ENTRANT FIXTURE COLUMN [--kind K] [--view V] [--flea TREE] [--preview MODE] [--out DIR] [--json FILE]

Launch columns ride the same plan: launch.first_frame.<size> is exec to the first presented frame
of the window at all, launch.first_rows.<size> exec to the first frame whose content region shows
rows (ink rows at or over INK_ROWS, default the search tool's VISIBLE_ROWS 25), each beside
launch.settled.<size>, the last change before 2 s of quiet, cap 15 s. One full-output recorder
(bar masked) runs from exec; geometry read at map decides which frames belonged to the window.
Cold is prepared by the caller (page and thumbnail caches dropped before the run); the plan stamps
"cache": "cold" or "warm" in the manifest so a number is never read without its cache state.

The method is tools/flea-field-search's: tools/flea-framecap records which presented frames differ
in a rectangle, stamped with the compositor's presentation time in CLOCK_MONOTONIC, and keys are
written to the ydotool socket stamped in CLOCK_MONOTONIC just before the write, so key and frame
share one clock. This tool imports that file (SourceFileLoader, no copy) and reuses its detector,
input path, recorder, launch lines, regions and report maths. Columns, each the keystroke to the
first frame in which the entrant's content region changes (first) and to the last change before
2 s of quiet, cap 15 s (settled): nav.cursor.inview.<view> (one untimed Down, quiet, then 7 timed
Downs at a 400 ms pace that stay inside the first screen), nav.cursor.scroll.<view> (Downs past the
bottom edge, quiet, then 12 timed Downs that each scroll), nav.enter.<view> and nav.back.<view>
(one Down selects the folder, quiet, Enter into its 1000 entries, quiet, the back key out), preview.<kind>
(quicklook: Space on the file; pane: the Down that lands on it, watched in the preview heuristic
region, the right 40 percent of the content region, refined per entrant with explore).
An entrant without the preview feature gets a "no feature" row, never a silent gap.
The NAV key table's copies live under .flea-local/ref/apps/ and are close to the installed
versions; every chord is checked on the operator's box with explore before measuring, and a
copy that differs is re-cited there. The pane preview's stimulus is the cursor move that lands
on the file: the last Down of the walk there, or an Up back to row 0 when the file is first.
Sample input, one recorder line: "F 660389861257350 660389874933379 32 95 126" (presentation ns, received ns, rows).
Sample plan: {"out": "o.jsonl", "runs": 5, "fixtures": {"nav500": "D/nav500"}, "arms": [{"id": "f", "entrant": "flea"}]}.
Sample row: {"arm": "f", "column": "nav.cursor.inview.list", "per_key_first_ms": [4.4, 4.7], "settled_ms": 40.1}.
"""
